	(text "HARNESS J1: every field wire enters on one Molex Micro-Fit 3.0 plug (Teltonika-style harness).\nJ1 = 2x8 right-angle header 43045-1600 (LCSC C277731), 3.00 mm pitch, assembled by JLCPCB.\nCable side, orderable from LCSC with the board order: receptacle 43025-1600 (C293527)\n+ 16 female crimp terminals 43030-0007 (C293530) for 20-24 AWG wire.\nCrimp with a Micro-Fit / MX3.0 ratchet crimper (e.g. Molex 63819-0000). MX3.0-compatible housings and terminals also mate."
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "479547cb-1d8e-414a-881a-55a1b90f6c95")
	)
	(text "Row 1, pins 1-8 (front row, under the housing)\n1  GND (battery negative)\n2  GND (signal return: sensors, RS232, RS485, CAN)\n3  RS232 TX (out, +/-70 V tolerant)\n4  +5 V out, 200 mA (F801), for sensors\n5  CAN_L\n6  RS485 B\n7  DIN COM = VEH_GND (isolated DIN return)\n8  DIN COM = VEH_GND (second return wire)"
		(at 25.4 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3c090c91-bd15-4df7-be91-50f5b667d69d")
	)
	(text "Row 2, pins 9-16 (back row)\n9   VIN 9-30 V (inline 1 A fuse at the battery)\n10  DOUT1 open drain, 0.5 A (load from +V to pin 10)\n11  AIN1 0-30 V (4-20 mA with R904 fitted)\n12  RS232 RX (in, +/-70 V tolerant)\n13  CAN_H\n14  RS485 A\n15  DIN1 (alternator L / D+ or oil-pressure switch)\n16  DIN2 (pulse input)"
		(at 116.84 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e0c0405d-8031-410e-97e4-4fb07c3f2947")
	)
	(text "Pin order: the five vehicle-voltage nets (VIN, DOUT1, AIN1, DIN1, DIN2) sit on the back row and leave the header straight back.\nTheir 0.8 mm Vehicle clearance leaves no room for a track between two of them (the pad gap is 1.5 mm), so each front-row signal\nleaves between a back-row pin pair that holds at most one vehicle net. The signals then leave J1 in module order, top to bottom:\nRS485 A, B | CAN_L, CAN_H | +5 V | RS232 RX, TX | AIN1 | DOUT1 | VIN, so no two modules' tracks cross.\nEvery pair of neighbouring pins survives a short: +5 V (4) only touches RS232 TX (3), CAN_L (5) and RS232 RX (12), all rated\n+/-58 V or more; DOUT1 (10) sits between VIN and AIN1, across GND (2). The isolated DIN group (7, 8, 15, 16) fills the pin 8/16 end.\nNot isolated: GND is the vehicle ground. Only DIN1/DIN2 are isolated; their return is pin 7 or 8, never a GND pin."
		(at 25.4 71.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "918348f6-2808-4f26-95f7-f7f2e95a8430")
	)
